      "writtenOn": "2024-07-30T00:37:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "tiny nit: the name `arr` doesn\u0027t really obviously pair with `bufferOffset`. Also, any value is an offset--this is the _base_ offset.\n\nIdeas:\n\n- `arr` and `arrBase`? \n- `buffer` and `bufferBase`?\n- Simplify: `buffer` and `base`?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 642,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 642,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "8a91d3f487402f295a7b7af2cfcc1a9d30a08ccf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ce118f80_0f5f68f1",
        "filename": "src/sksl/sksl_graphite_frag.sksl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 642,
      "author": {
        "id": 3438316
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-30T20:00:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I actually kept `arr` as `arr` but changed `bufferOffset` to `offsetsBaseIndex` to signify this is where the stop offsets data begins. Then under it changed `colorOffset` to `colorsBaseIndex` so fetching stop offset data can be `arr[offsetsBaseIndex + x]` and color data being `$half4_from_array(colorsBaseIndex + x)`",
      "parentUuid": "c91fcb57_89c2d4e0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 642,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 642,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "8a91d3f487402f295a7b7af2cfcc1a9d30a08ccf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "54da2c65_e1e9e821",
        "filename": "src/sksl/sksl_graphite_frag.sksl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 642,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-30T20:13:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this helped readability for me. There\u0027s nothing that suggests upon casual inspection that `arr` and `offsetsBaseIndex` are related, and `offsetsBaseIndex` is wordy. \n\nIn other words: there are too many things called \"offset\" here. We need to avoid calling everything an offset or readability suffers.",
      "parentUuid": "ce118f80_0f5f68f1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 642,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 642,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "8a91d3f487402f295a7b7af2cfcc1a9d30a08ccf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
